{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol."}],"metadata":{"title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","externalID":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","modules":[{"name":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"}],"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") for a Google Analytics 4 stream in one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call. It checks the measurement ID and the API secret, and posts to the Measurement Protocol’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/mp\/collect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint of the region (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion"},{"text":") with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"},{"text":". It splits each batch to the Measurement Protocol’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":"): 25 events and 100 KB a request. A batch with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"The API secret stays on a server","anchor":"The-API-secret-stays-on-a-server"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol takes only requests that carry one of the stream’s API secrets, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyone holding that secret can send events to the property. Google’s docs say not to expose it in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an app, and an app’s binary can be read by anyone who installs it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So the whole module is compiled for macOS and Linux alone, where a server runs. An app for iOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iPadOS, tvOS, watchOS, visionOS or Mac Catalyst that calls the factory, or names the encoder, fails","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to compile. A Mac app, AppKit or SwiftUI, compiles the factory as a Mac server does, but the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factory refuses it at run time: it throws ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError\/appBundle","isActive":true},{"text":" when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"process’s main bundle is an ","type":"text"},{"code":".app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"code":".appex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Nothing stops a Mac app from building an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with this encoder and an endpoint it writes itself, secret and all, so don’t.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The secret is also in the query of every request’s URL. Don’t log the destination, its requests or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a transport’s URLs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for an empty measurement ID, for one that isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G-"},{"type":"text","text":" followed by uppercase letters and digits, and for an empty API secret. The region has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".global"},{"type":"text","text":" is Google’s default endpoint, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".eu"},{"type":"text","text":" has Google collect the data in the EU."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Getting an app’s events to Google Analytics","anchor":"Getting-an-apps-events-to-Google-Analytics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An app’s events reach Google Analytics through a server of yours: the app sends them there, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the server makes this destination and hands it the records. Traffluent doesn’t provide that server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yet. TraffluentCollector receives an app’s batches, but it doesn’t forward them to Google","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Analytics, and Traffluent has no decoder that turns a collector batch back into records.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Until it does, the server’s job is:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Read each event the app sent (its name, version, identifier, timestamp, properties and session)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and decode it into the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" type the app tracked, from a module the app and the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Remake its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord(id:event:timestamp:sourceLocation:context:)"},{"text":": the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app’s identifier and timestamp, and a context whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":" is the app’s session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand each batch of records to the destination’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"receive(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t track the events again through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":".sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the server. That tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would give every event the server’s own session, so every user of the app would arrive in Google","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Analytics as one ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A server that tracks its own events, rather than an app’s, uses a tracker as any app does:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let googleAnalytics = try HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(","    measurementID: measurementID,  \/\/ the web or data stream's, G-…","    apiSecret: apiSecret,  \/\/ from the server's configuration, never an app's","    region: .global,  \/\/ or .eu, to have Google collect the data in the EU","    plan: plan)","\/\/ A server tracking its own events: its sessions are the server's.","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: googleAnalytics)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Google Analytics receives","anchor":"What-Google-Analytics-receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request holds one client’s events, as the Measurement Protocol takes one ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, written as the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"halves of its UUID in decimal, joined by a period, the form the Measurement Protocol asks for. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, in a request of its own. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter is the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, so Google Analytics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"groups the session’s events, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp_micros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s timestamp. Every request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends ad consent as denied, so Google uses none of the events for advertising.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", user properties, location, IP address, device or user agent is sent, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"advertising identifier. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and standard context aren’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent either. Google Analytics counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports, and so is each record sent without a session."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"code":"engagement_time_msec","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent, as Traffluent doesn’t measure engagement. Without it the events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"don’t count toward engagement time or engaged sessions, and the Realtime and Users reports can show"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no users while events arrive. Check the event counts, not the user counts, to see that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination works."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and become the event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"params"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics takes only strings, numbers and booleans, so a nested value is spread into a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter for each value it holds, named after its path joined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart_size"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags_0"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records sent twice","anchor":"Records-sent-twice"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol has no field that identifies an event, so Google Analytics can’t tell a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"repeat from a new event, and counts every one it receives. A record is sent more than once when a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request is retried after Google stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancelled batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each such record is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counted twice in Google Analytics.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name, or a parameter’s name, is longer than 40 bytes, doesn’t start with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"letter, or holds anything but letters, numbers and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Google Analytics keeps ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_start"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"first_visit"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its reserved names), or takes only from an app stream ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_view"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_impression"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in_app_purchase"},{"type":"text","text":");"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a parameter Google Analytics keeps (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"firebase_"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ga_"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"google_"},{"type":"text","text":" prefix) or named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which the encoder writes;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one of more than 25 parameters, counting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", or with a string longer than 100 bytes;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one tracked more than 72 hours before the batch is encoded, or more than 15 minutes after it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one whose timestamp has no microseconds form;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one too large for a request."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics wouldn’t refuse such an event: it answers 2xx either way. Under its default,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relaxed validation it stores the event without the parameter that breaks a rule, or under a name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it never checked, so the report would hold an event other than the one tracked. The encoder leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the record out and reports it instead. A Google Analytics 360 property takes values of up to 500"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters, but the encoder holds every property to the standard 100 bytes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The encoder logs a notice for each event and property of the plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"named as Google Analytics refuses when the destination is made; rename such an event or property,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raising the event’s version, to send it."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What the Measurement Protocol doesn’t report","anchor":"What-the-Measurement-Protocol-doesnt-report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it receives, including one it can’t read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose events it doesn’t store. A wrong measurement ID or API secret is answered 2xx with nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored, so check the property’s Realtime event counts after setting the destination up. Google’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validation server, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/debug\/mp\/collect"},{"text":", checks a body’s shape but not the measurement ID or the API","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"secret, so a body it accepts can still be stored nowhere. A record older than 72 hours is stored as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"if it happened 72 hours ago, so the encoder leaves those out too; a request retried for long after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its batch was encoded can still arrive past that window.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel or Segment, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentSpecEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Google Analytics receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Google-Analytics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Google Analytics"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol’s limits on one request: 25 events and 100,000 bytes of body, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s included.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"batchLimit","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/batchlimit"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError/appBundle":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"appBundle","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError\/appBundle","title":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError.appBundle","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The process is an app or an app extension: its main bundle is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".app"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".appex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directory. The factory is compiled for macOS so a server written for it can run there, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mac app compiles it too, but an app ships the API secret to everyone who installs it, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyone holding the secret can send events to the property. Send the app’s events to a relay"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of yours instead, which forwards them to Google Analytics."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticssetuperror\/appbundle","type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A destination on a server that sends batches to the Google Analytics web or data stream of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"measurementID"},{"text":", authenticated by its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"apiSecret"},{"text":", through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"text":", retrying a send that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"googleAnalytics","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"measurementID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"apiSecret","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"region","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB6RegionO","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transport","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"now","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","text":"Date","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB10SetupErrorO","text":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdenti